<title>RUSSIA: Russian 357-day T-bills yield 31.01 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 357-day T-bills yield 31.01 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 357-day GKO discount Treasury bills was 31.01 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the average yield would be in the 32-38 percent range. Full details of the auction follow:</p>
<p>    Series number	     23002</p>
<p>    Issue volume		7.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations	     1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	   12.23 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	    6.94 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		    5.33 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	     76.73 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price   76.73 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	     31.01 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield  31.01 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			 357 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date	     Feb 18, 1998</p>
<p>On February 26, the Finance Ministry will offer 4.50 trillion roubles ($793 million) in 91-day T-bills (series 21072).</p>
<p>It will also pay about 687.12 billion roubles in interest on maturing OFZ interest-bearing bonds (series 24003) and redeem the entire issue, in which 6.88 trillion roubles is outstanding. It will also pay about 329.48 billion roubles in interest on the series 24004 OFZ bonds.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520 ($ = 5675 Russian Roubles)</p>
